css='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;padding:35px;background:#faf8f4;color:#293229;font:15px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1480px;margin:auto}h1{font:46px Georgia}h2{font:30px Georgia}a{color:#3f5e51}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:25px}.pair figure{margin:0}.pair img{display:block;width:100%;height:470px;object-fit:cover;object-position:top;border:1px solid #74816c}.pair figcaption{padding:15px 0;font-size:13px}section{border-top:1px solid #c9cec5;padding:30px 0}dt{font-weight:bold}dd{margin:0 0 12px;max-width:1000px}.note{color:#596754;font-size:13px}@media(max-width:700px){body{padding:22px}.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:36px}}'''
b='<main><a href="../index.html">← Dewdrop storybook</a><h1>Conventions retained.<br>A different care-shopping task.</h1><p>Original design comparison, dated 22 October 2026. Both desktop sources were rendered at 1440 × 1000 CSS px, DPR 1. Previews below show the opening crop; open the full source image for all content. Shopify screenshots are research evidence, never theme assets.</p>'
for x in records:
 b+=f'<section><h2>{x["reference"]} / Dewdrop — {x["scene"]}</h2><div class="pair"><figure><a href="{x["referenceImage"]}"><img src="{x["referenceImage"]}" alt="Saved {x["reference"]} primary-source screenshot"></a><figcaption><a href="{x["url"]}">{x["reference"]} public demo</a> · {x["state"]}<br>Saved capture: 2026-10-22 / 1440 × 1000 / DPR 1</figcaption></figure><figure><a href="../images/{x["scene"]}-desktop.png"><img src="../images/{x["scene"]}-desktop.png" alt="Dewdrop {x["scene"]}"></a><figcaption>Dewdrop design v1 · 2026-10-23 export · {x["scene"]}<br>1440 × 1000 viewport / full-page PNG / DPR 1</figcaption></figure></div><dl><dt>User problem</dt><dd>{x["problem"]}</dd><dt>Retained convention</dt><dd>{x["retained"]}</dd><dt>Original departure and reason</dt><dd>{x["difference"]}</dd><dt>Required contract</dt><dd>{x["contract"]}</dd></dl><p class="note">{x["evidence"]} {x["evidenceLimits"]}</p></section>'
b+='</main>'
(R/'side-by-side.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Dewdrop research comparisons</title><style>'+css+'</style>'+b+'</html>')
neutral='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Dewdrop neutral task structure</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;padding:40px;font:15px/1.5 Arial;color:#222;background:#fff}main{max-width:1320px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:32px}h2{font-size:22px}.columns{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:30px}.frame{border:2px solid #555;padding:20px}.block{border:1px solid #999;background:#f3f3f3;padding:16px;margin:14px 0}.media{height:95px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,#f5f5f5,#f5f5f5 8px,#ddd 8px,#ddd 9px);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px}.row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:70px 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:center}.row .media{height:90px}.step{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:start}.number{font-size:25px;font-weight:bold}.three{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:7px}.pill{border:1px solid #555;padding:8px;font-size:12px}p{font-size:13px}.label{font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px}.foot{margin-top:30px;border-top:1px solid #aaa;padding-top:20px}@media(max-width:750px){.columns{grid-template-columns:1fr}body{padding:20px}}</style><main><a href="../index.html">← Storybook</a><h1>Does the task survive without colour or photography?</h1><p>Original diagrams, not modified remote pages. Branding, accent colour and photographic imagery are suppressed. These describe planned LetBuyy structures from the portfolio research, not certified user outcomes.</p><div class="columns"><section><h2>Dewdrop / care</h2><div class="frame"><div class="label">Use-led opening</div><div class="block">What step are you choosing?<div class="three"><span class="pill">Cleanse</span><span class="pill">Care</span><span class="pill">Colour</span></div></div><div class="block step"><span class="number">01</span><div><b>Rinse-off shelf</b><p>Independent product + type + net quantity + price</p></div></div><div class="block step"><span class="number">02</span><div><b>Leave-on shelf</b><p>Directions / ingredients supplied?</p></div></div><div class="block step"><span class="number">03</span><div><b>Named shade shelf</b><p>Same colour, distinct name and variant ID</p></div></div><div class="block"><b>Product decision</b><p>Gallery → named shade radios → ingredients + use → quantity / buy</p><div class="three"><span class="pill">Rosewater<br>RW01</span><span class="pill">Pink Clay<br>PC02</span><span class="pill">Unavailable</span></div></div></div><p>Primary uncertainty: what it contains, how to use it, which shade is selected.</p></section><section><h2>Pantry / packaged food</h2><div class="frame"><div class="label">Compact seasonal entry</div><div class="block">Food type / pack-size browsing</div><div class="block row"><div class="media">Pack</div><div><b>Staple row</b><p>Net weight / pack count / unit price</p><span class="pill">− 2 packs +</span></div></div><div class="block row"><div class="media">Pack</div><div><b>Ingredient row</b><p>Allergens / storage / preparation</p><span class="pill">Add known SKU</span></div></div><div class="block"><b>Product decision</b><p>Ingredients + supplied allergens → net quantity / pack facts → purchase</p></div></div><p>Primary uncertainty: allergens, food quantity, pack count and storage. No shade selection.</p></section><section><h2>Threadline / clothing</h2><div class="frame"><div class="label">Silhouette / editorial entry</div><div class="media">Portrait campaign</div><div class="three block"><div class="media">Portrait</div><div class="media">Portrait</div><div class="media">Portrait</div></div><div class="block"><b>Product decision</b><p>Garment gallery → named colour → size → fit / measurements → buy</p><div class="three"><span class="pill">S</span><span class="pill">M</span><span class="pill">L</span></div></div><div class="block">Fabric / care → independent outfit items</div></div><p>Primary uncertainty: garment measurements, silhouette and fabric. Portraits do not substitute for fit facts.</p></section></div><div class="foot"><b>Meaningful difference:</b> care separates routine stage, use, ingredients and shade identity; food makes food quantity/allergen facts primary; fashion makes garment fit and size primary. Shared selection/cart mechanics remain familiar.<p>Source: 06_TEN_NICHE_PORTFOLIO.md, 08-aura-dewdrop.md and Threadline storybook. No copied layout or media. No conversion or full accessibility claim.</p></div></main></html>'''
(R/'neutral-structure.html').write_text(neutral)
